186045417] [17592186344778 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344778 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186342787 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344778 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "a1ed40d7-8e7a-5f9c-b818-44e52bc41e91" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344878 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186342524 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344878 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186342542 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344878 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186342627 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344878 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186342781 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344878 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186343678 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344878 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344878 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344878 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186343678 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344878 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "dd9d2ad5-13fa-5805-9e22-ef7e6b03da8a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345066 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186344778 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345066 #edb/ref 1069 "q-75317" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345066 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345066 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $R=[3,4]\\times [5,6]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=4{x}^{2}+7{y}^{2}-12.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the lower Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhere $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$ what is the missing expression in the double summation above?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345066 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "02670488-7066-5e84-b67c-68ab62041d19" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345066 #edb/ref 1074 "The lower Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ is the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion ${R}_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$ over the $x$-axis and ${y}_{i-1}$ and ${y}_{i}$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](images/88/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $f(x,y)=4{x}^{2}+7{y}^{2}-12$ increases as $x$ increases on $[3,4],$ and\n\n- $f(x,y)=4{x}^{2}+7{y}^{2}-12$ increases as $y$ increases on $[5,6].$\n\n![](images/67/67daa328cc6ae4cb37be386c327fb4548844fad2adc10476bdf1147c5a5d4218.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom left corner* of each subregion. \n\n![](images/51/51808df96cf7dd295bfa24aa3641a601c821116e1a0014898ffe705036704a53.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i-1},{y}_{j-1})=4{x}_{i-1}^{2}+7{y}_{j-1}^{2}-12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\le i\\le m$ and $1\\le j\\le n.$\n\nFinally, the lower Riemann sum is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(4{x}_{i-1}^{2}+7{y}_{j-1}^{2}-12)Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is $4{x}_{i-1}^{2}+7{y}_{j-1}^{2}-12.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345068 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186344577 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345068 #edb/ref 1069 "q-75319" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345068 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345068 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $R=[1,5]\\times [-2,-1]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=11x+2y-6.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the lower Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhere $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$ what is the missing expression in the double summation above?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345068 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7ab122c6-4ba8-55ac-a470-6de6531010b5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345068 #edb/ref 1074 "The lower Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ is the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion ${R}_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$ over the $x$-axis and ${y}_{i-1}$ and ${y}_{i}$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](images/88/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $f(x,y)=11x+2y-6$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=11x+2y-6$ increases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/67/67daa328cc6ae4cb37be386c327fb4548844fad2adc10476bdf1147c5a5d4218.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom left corner* of each subregion. \n\n![](images/51/51808df96cf7dd295bfa24aa3641a601c821116e1a0014898ffe705036704a53.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i-1},{y}_{j-1})=11{x}_{i-1}+2{y}_{j-1}-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\le i\\le m$ and $1\\le j\\le n.$\n\nFinally, the lower Riemann sum is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(11{x}_{i-1}+2{y}_{j-1}-6)Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is $11{x}_{i-1}+2{y}_{j-1}-6.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345069 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186344611 #edb/ref 175921